{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511673-giving-background-to-the-3rd-generation","id":1511673,"title":"Giving background to the 3rd generation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-14T17:00:16-07:00","id":1511673,"title":"Giving background to the 3rd generation","content":"I saw some people interested in the personality of the antediluvians and how it would impact the relationships they have with each other, thinking about it I did this. I don't know if this will do anything, but I think it would be a good exercise at the very least, I'll post other things as ideas come.<br /> <br /> Brujah: He has a veiled hatred towards most other antediluvians, the only ones he partially tolerates are, ironically, Ventrue and Cappadocian, he considers Saulot a hypocrite.<br /> <br /> Troile: Sees the other antediluvians as enemies to be eventually diablerized, the only ones he would consider allying with would be Ennoia and Haqim, even that would be temporary. He considers Nosferatu dangerous, Ventrue and Lasombra just arrogant old ones, Set, Malkav and Saulot crazy and totally unpredictable, Tzimice doesn't even seem kindred in his eyes and Giovanni as the least threat.<br /> <br /> Ennoia: Cares little for her siblings these days, but she once had respect for Nosferatu even though she was never particularly close to him, she always avoided Cappadocian due to their different interests, and Malkav due to his unstable mind. She never had the patience to deal with Ventrue, Lasombra or Brujah, although she could if had to, the only one she really hated was Tzimice, as she doesn't consider him a brother, just one \u201cthing\u201d and even that title doesn't seem right. The only one she shows real indifference to is Goratrix.<br /> <br /> Absimiliard: He seems to hate most of his brothers, the only one with whom he has a \u201cfriendly\u201d relationship is Toreador, he also maintains a relationship of some respect with Ennoia, perhaps because she doesn\u2019t seem to him an immediate threat. Regarding his other brothers, some that deserve mention are Tzimice, Malkav and Brujah for different reasons, Brujah, because his unique discipline always eluded his understanding and he could never think of a realistic way to deal with it and he doesn't believe in his death either, think like that certainty is not a luxury he can afford; In the case of Malkav, in the view of Nosferatu all living beings or that were once alive always surrender to their habits and if you know these habits you won\u2019t need to fear any beast, but Malkav is a unique creature that escapes this rule, his personality is ever-changing which makes him very difficult to deal with, Tzimice is a similar case but different in his own way, as due to his unique discipline he is ever-changing and whenever he change his way of thinking seemed to change a little with him.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T17:38:13-07:00","id":1511682,"title":"","content":"Set views most his fellow 3rd generation siblings as rivals in his desire to remake the world in his own image. But he really detests Ventrue the most he is the only one who could rival in natural leadership skills and ambition. Lasombra he vaguely admires for his ruthlessness and not much else. Toreador doesn\u2019t even register on his radar and views her harmless for the most part. The only one he views as a real friend is Malkav for reasons he can\u2019t really explain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T17:45:46-07:00","id":1511683,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't focus so much on what they think about each other, but on their personality, current status, long term goals and strategies used. <br /> For example:<br /> Ennoia&gt; She is an eternal wanderer, who has travelled all around the world once and once again and never gets tired. She has experienced it as a woman, as a wolf, as a bird, as a bat, as part of earth itself. She dislikes the Jyhad, buy has seen her siblings won't stop playing and are ready to even destroy the world in order to achieve victory. She also dislikes cities and would like to stop civilization on its tracks. Throughout history she has used her Children to infiltrate and stir up chaos through the Huns, the Mongols, the Vandals, but she has realised that tactic is useless in a time of nuclear weapons, and is instead playing a subtler game, trying to give strength to pacifist and nuclear desarment groups while her Clan tries to play the political game in all sects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-15T00:13:55-07:00","id":1511699,"title":"","content":"Before the followers<br /> <br /> Set knew that nothing would ever be the same, what he and his brothers had done there was no going back, but they didn't imagine the extent of Cain's fury. Now that everything was over, it was time to start over, look for another place, without a certain destination Set was reunited with his brother, Malkav, for some reason disguised as a woman, he was good at imitating other people, but there was no way he could deceive his brothers and he wasn't even trying. With his company the two traveled aimlessly, they couldn't stay long in one place, Set wondered how long it would be like this, one night the two stopped in a cave, Malkav spoke of a land where Set would find his destiny, he still he didn't know, but that was how it all started, Malkav disappeared that night. Years later Set was faced with his purpose and he was not the only one, many followed him in this new venture, but not everything is flowers, from the mouths of outsiders he heard legends and stories of monsters and disasters that couldn\u2019t be from anyone less than his brothers, just one more reason not to stay quiet, to survive he needed power and for that he needed minions, followers capable of dying for him, soon he found himself trying to gift others with his power and his first chosen one was a woman who joined recently, she was just like Malkav, to be exact she was just like his brother's disguise years ago when he told him that prophecy, Set thought to himself: how much more did he know?<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-15T16:58:17-07:00","id":1511751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511673-giving-background-to-the-3rd-generation?p=1511683#post1511683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't focus so much on what they think about each other, but on their personality, current status, long term goals and strategies used.<br /> For example:<br /> Ennoia&gt; She is an eternal wanderer, who has travelled all around the world once and once again and never gets tired. She has experienced it as a woman, as a wolf, as a bird, as a bat, as part of earth itself. She dislikes the Jyhad, buy has seen her siblings won't stop playing and are ready to even destroy the world in order to achieve victory. She also dislikes cities and would like to stop civilization on its tracks. Throughout history she has used her Children to infiltrate and stir up chaos through the Huns, the Mongols, the Vandals, but she has realised that tactic is useless in a time of nuclear weapons, and is instead playing a subtler game, trying to give strength to pacifist and nuclear desarment groups while her Clan tries to play the political game in all sects.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that more important than their relationship with the other Antediluvians is their plan concerning the Jyhad. What are their methods and how they expect to emerge victorious in the conflict through these methods, etc. How do they plan to win and to keep their rule is something very interesting to explore, also is giving them backgrounds like features, e.g. merits and flaws, for instance and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-16T01:23:06-07:00","id":1511778,"title":"","content":"<b>Ilyes</b><br /> In the Second City, He had the reputation of being cold and passionless, Troile - whose gender is ambiguous, was known for being a passionate and fiery person, in stark contrast to that of their sire - Troile was Embraced by the &quot;Learned&quot;, sometime around 3000 BCE.<br /> According to the Tzimisce Clanbook, Mekhet was a sibling of the Eldest (and thus possibly another childe of Ynosh/Enoch) who, with the Brujah antediluvian &quot;played shadow games with mortals, delighting in their own cunning and agendas&quot;<br /> \u200bThere is a little inconsistency In DAV: Road of Humanity, the Prodigals told of a story in which Arikel and Troile were troubled by the way the Cainites of the <i>First City</i> behaved, and turned to Saulot for aid. The Healer stated that only empathy would help them retain a link to humanity and so, both Troile and Arikel went to work on a project of art that spanned a hundred and one years, before they brought it before Caine. The work inspired exactly those emotions within the audience that they had inspired in the mortal population. Caine was deeply touched by it and called Arikel and Troile to his side, forgiving them past trespasses. These prodigals hold this as the origin of the Road of Humanity<br /> That is not really a question, Troile was Embraced in the Second City, so the Troile in the First City was porbably Ilyes - Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand and Gehenna refer to Troile as female, suggesting that Her Sire was in love with her, but could not express it as he knew not how to deal with his emotions.<br /> It actually fits nicely in the whole picture<br /> At first, back in the old days, Ilyies and Arikel had a working relationship, so to speak, both interested in Mortals.As well as he had a working relationship with Mekhet, whom he &quot;played shadow games with mortals, delighting in their own cunning and agendas&quot; - from a Vulcan-like cold and passionate point of view this could mean experiments, cruel and cold social experiments and so on; the; the project of art that spanned a hundred and one years coud be from his early days, when he was freshly Embraced and still had that spark in him... and gradually lost it. But trusted Sualot enough to turn to him with his concerns.<br /> Ilyies was allegedly slain by his childe, Troile, who may have committed diablerie on him in the process BUT some Brujah, such as a commentator on the Erciyes Fragments, believe that his death was a lie spread by the Ventrue.<br /> In Gehenna's &quot;general description&quot; some stories, however, claim that Troile and [Brujah] had been the same person, as few to no records exist that place them together, and that [Brujah] faked his own destruction and assumed Troile's identity. (also in Gehenna the scenario &quot;Fair is Foul&quot; reintroduces Brujah to the childer of Caine under the name of Ilyes. Here, Ilyes faked his own death; having complete mastery over time, he escaped his destruction, using his trademark Discipline, Temporis,)<br /> Clanbook: Brujah Revised mentions records claiming Troile had no gender or changed it on whim.<br /> <br /> When he is not escaped via Temporis, peronally I tend to go with the later version; a bit headcanon, but could work. So, Embrace, especially Embracing your lover was a direct violation of Caine's dictum. Because of Ilyes's lack of emotion - or more precisely, he could not express his love as he knew not how to deal with his emotions - Troile feared that her Sire had the intention to destroy them, in an attempt to rectify his mistake of Embracing progeny. Thus, Troile paniced and attacked his Sire. Who consumed Her. And the act shattered his already unstable mind and assumed Her identity. A bit of reverse Mithras-Monthy-way. This would explain why Troile wasn't punished with final death for the Diablerie. It not happened. The others looked the confused and bloody mouthed Ilyies and pitied him, who began to pretend he was Troile. Even some crossdressing could have been in play. The &quot;had no gender or changed it on whim&quot; part could be viewed as the vampire basically genderlessness, since they are dead bodies, like Angels, basically have no gender, just gender identity.<br /> From there, he was Troile<br /> <br /> The official version according to clan Ventrue members states that theri Antediluvian may have been destroyed outside of the walls of the Second City by the Brujah antediluvian... which is firmly denied by the Brujah Clan. So probably it not really happened, since the Venture Antediluvian was Embracing left and right later on...<br /> <br /> <b>Troile</b><br /> Picking up from the previous entry, according Clan Book: Baali, among his brethren, Nergal was the one most adept at dealing with other Cainites. It is said that he served as Arikel's wench, debated philosophy with Troile and traded vice secrets with the Tzimisce Antediluvian<br /> Within Carthage, Moloch became a confidant to Troile, knowing of his dark hunger and encouraging this aspect in him. Soon, Baali became one of the most influential vampiric lines within the city, demanding blood sacrifices and worship from the mortal inhabitants. Under Moloch's influence, Troile became much more moody, draining his enemies of their vitae and Embracing childer just to devour them. In time, the two became lovers, unknown to the rest of Moloch's brood.<br /> In 146 BCE, Troile participated in the final battle of Carthage.<br /> According to the Baali, Troile descended into the earth, presumably using Protean, in an Embrace with its lover Moloch (a Baali methuselah), in order to hide from the Roman attackers. The vampires of Rome had the ground sown with salt and enacted a ritual that locked Troile and Moloch beneath the earth in eternal torpor.<br /> <br /> <b>Sargon of Cappadocia</b><br /> The names of most of the third generation are lost to history, but Cappadocius' name is unknown even to his contemporaries. To hear Cappadocian scholars tell it, the priest who would become Cappadocius chose to abandon his original name and take this one even before his Embrace, and this is the only name he offered to Caine and the second generation. Some even say that Cappadocius goes by no true name because he himself no longer knows it! In his days as a mortal priest and man of faith, Cappadocius had his own dealings with the dead, a conversation here and there with spirits of those gone, and he had made several enemies in his time. When the Antediluvian died briefly during the Embrace, those spirits were waiting for him in the lands Beneath, and they attempted to cling to him, to prevent him from returning to his body when the curse of Caine took hold. It is said that, to some extent, they succeeded. Part of Cappadocius never returned from the underworld. Much of his knowledge and self-awareness were lost in that faulty Embrace, and the being who returned was not quite he who began the journey. Cappadocius' very soul had been fragmented, and that is why he harbored such a fascination for the dead: Even when he himself did not realize it, he was constantly seeking the missing portions of himself. His progeny speculate that this flawed Embrace is also the reason for Cappadocius' deathly appearance; because the spirit that returned to his body was incomplete, it was unable to fully stave off the decay of the grave. It may also be the reason that Augustus Giovanni could not devour his soul completely, as a part of it had always been in the Underworld. In any event, Cappadocius spent most of his time in the Second City seeking answers to his various and sundry questions of the nature of life and death, studying ways to question the spirits, and \u2013 in his spare time \u2013 advising the other Cainites on any matters about which they chose to query him.<br /> Interesting to mention the alias &quot;Laodice&quot; - the sire of the Cappadocian Byzar/Mahatma in Children of the Night. The choice of the name Laodice is particularly interesting as it is a <i>feminine </i>name, suggesting Cappadocius may have taken on different forms as well as different names.<br /> The Second Revelation of Cappadocius was a vision of himself on the Cross, mirroring the crucification of Christ and his eventual ascension to Heaven. Cappadocius believed that he had to become God in order to sustain humanity in the face of an ever-growing vampire population. To reach this goal, Cappadocius and his closest childer studied mortal religions until the Clan Founder became convinced that, if he used a ritual that would involve his own sacrifice, he could diablerize God Himself. With this power, he would bring Heaven \u2013 the afterlife \u2013 on Earth by eliminating the boundaries between life and death itself. All creatures would lead perfect, unchanging lifes without pain or need under his benevolent rule. Cappadocius' efforts became more and more erratic after he witnessed the betrayal of Augustus Giovanni in a vision, believing that the Necromancer would fulfill his role by slaying his corporal form, allowing his soul to consume God. When Augustus eventually acted on his desire in 1444, Cappadocius awaited the deed, offering little resistance. Both of them failed in their aspirations<br /> Cappadocius found that he did not reach Heaven, instead emerging as a wraith in the Shadowlands. He watched the ages pass and his Clan die, powerless to act, until the Fifth Maelstrom sucked him into the Labyrinth, which he left in 1998 as a Spectre.<br /> <br /> <b>Ennoia</b><br /> There are many different versions on who exactly Ennoia was, the fractured nature of the Clan making a depiction much more difficult<br /> The name Ennoia means &quot;the female half of God&quot;, and it is said she was a child of Lilith. However, she was abandoned by her mother to a pack of wolves. The animals raised her to become a great predatory hunter. According to Lord Ashton (a 10th Generation Gangrel expert in Gangrel lore and a Anarch storyteller): &quot;Ennoia took a mate from the pack and... bore him children... and it is from them that Lupines trace their ancestry&quot;. - This is probably not true. Or who knows, if you are not in to mixing game lines could work<br /> Legend has it that Ennoia and Ravana were siblings. After all the fallout of the Second City, the siblings wandered westward onto the vast steppe of central Asia. While Ennoia established her time in Sumer, Ravana encountered native tribes, mostly nomads and wanderers. They Embraced childer, known as methuselahs of the Gangrel and Ravnos clans. A reference to a &quot;Great Spider King&quot; and a &quot;Tiger Queen&quot; was found on a pre-Alexandrian inscription deep within an empty tomblike cave, on the shores of the Caspian Sea. Some Gangrel scholars are led to believe that the Spider King was Ravana, and Ennoia the Tiger Queen. Eventually, Ennoia and Ravana had a falling out. Something happened to drive them to one another's throats. They fought for decades; they flung their childer at one another, and even encouraged their childer to Embrace new fledglings as soldiers. By all accounts, Ennoia's broods were far stronger, but Ravana was far more cunning and wielded the powers of deception. At last, Ravana called down some kind of unholy devastation from the sky to destroy or disable most of Ennoia's forces. The handful that survived fled west<br /> A story told by the Indian Ravnos in their holy text, the Karavalashina Vrana, the Gangrel Antediluvian (also named Ennoia) was created by the gods as a second undead monster next to Zapathasura. She is called the most dangerous of warriors, supposedly mastering the art of shapeshifting in order to better combat the asuratizayya. When the gods told her the price of her existence, she cursed them for making her an unliving beast and turned her back on the duties they had charged her to fulfill. Enraged, the gods cursed their second creation to &quot;dwell among the beasts and find no safe haven anywhere in the world.&quot; They also gave her bestial features, so that no human would be deceived by her appearance. Following texts relate how the Gangrel, enraged at their loss of purpose, cannot abide the sight of the Ravnos for showing the strength and resolve Ennoia lacked and continue to harass them out of hate born out of shame.<br /> \u200bClanbook: Ravnos, speaks of the Rom as outcasts of the First City and of Ravnos as the favored childe of Caine. The history of the Rom begins as wanderers and outcasts of the Enoch, the First City. One family of these Romani was known as the Powara and were kinfolk of the descendants of Sarrath, werewolves that would later be known as the Silent Striders. One night during their travels, the youngest daughter of the Powara's leader, Laetshi, invited a stranger to camp with them. The man introduced himself as Caine, though he would be called Kaen in the Powara tongue. The Lupines that had long lived alongside the Powara refused to welcome Kaen amongst them, but for the time being they tolerated his presence. During the months that Kaen walked with the Powara, he came to be loved by them, particularly by their leader's son, an adolescent boy named Ravnos who was filled with the passions and dreams of youth. When his father was killed by wandering vampires, Ravnos pleaded with Kaen to give his father eternal life, but upon realizing that was not possible, Ravnos instead accepted the Embrace himself. The story continues to speak of the meeting of Ravnos and Ennoia, who would eventually betray him and bring about his death. Guided by Ravnos and his childer, the Rom eventually came to the Second City and made camp outside its walls. There Ravnos witnessed Ennoia being banished from the city, and he pitied her as one outcast for another. He welcomed Ennoia among his family, and over time they become close friends as they shared tales of their journeys, Embraced her and then became lovers as they made daring raids together to steal and beguile the Cainites of the Second City. But Ennoia grew bored of their time together, and endeavored to supplant him as leader of the Romani by handing Ravnos over to the leaders of the Second City. (I like to mention Dracian here; Dracian was the name of a thief that was Embraced by Irad in order to spy on the third generation. Irad suspected the other third generation neonates of plotting against the three members of the second generation and their sire. Dracian, for his part, took to the plot like a fish to water. He was at heart a selfish man, and becoming one of the typically selfish Cainite only deepened that trait. Before long, however, he joined the third generation cabal that sought the heart's blood of the second generation. It is said that Dracian was the one that tempted the Gangrel Antediluvian - so it is possible, Dracian conspired with Ennoia to kill he 2nd Generation Ravnos. Dracian, as punishment for his selfishness and short sightedness, was cursed to never know satisfaction. In search of that elusive quality, he followed the one member of the Third Generation who had not been cursed into the East, to seek what that other had allegedly found. He may indeed found it, becasue according to Roma lore, Dracian was the creator of a tree that was the embodiment life and knowledge, full in its age and beauty. It is said that one of the golden fruits of this Tree of Knowledge could cure the eternal thirst for blood in a vampire (as well as bestowing other unknown gifts))<br /> When Ravnos and Ennoia did not return from a foray into the city, Laetshi used her Sight to find them and witnessed the destruction of her brother as he was left tied atop the city's high temple to meet the sun's morning light. Furious with rage, Laetshi summoned her kin among the childer of Ravnos and the descendants of Sarrath so that they might subdue Ennoia. When Ennoia returned to the Romani camps, she was captured, and the Rom gathered to pass judgment upon her. According to the tale it was Kaen who would hand out punishment, however, joining the Rom's gathering to condemn the betrayer of his favorite son. Cursing Ennoia as a beast, Kaen placed upon her what would become the clan curse of all Gangrel. Condemned, Ennoia fled, but in her descendants a feud would continue to be waged between the Ravnos and Gangrel.<br /> Some Toreador scholars say She possessed the Tablet of Destiny until Ishtar tried to take the item from her. Outraged by this action, the Gangrel Antediluvian set out to kill Ishtar.<br /> As Ennoia tracked Ishtar to Sumer, she embraced Ereshkigal to help her in the attack on her sibling. When the Gangrel came to confront Ishtar, her childe-lover Tammuz interceded, and ultimately gave his unlife so that Ishtar could flee. She then sought aid from the king of Sumer, Gilgamesh. However, he had already been embraced by Ennoia. The Toreador fled from the pair, but not before unleashing upon them some great monster known as the Bull of Heaven, while she escaped to Crete.<br /> Ennoia decided to stay in Sumer, where she established a large brood of Gangrel.<br /> Under the guidance of their clan-founder, the Gangrel of the ancient city of Ur began training the man named Enkidu to be a childe of the Antediluvian, one that would be able to be the guardian of the several rare creatures contained by the Antediluvian within its flesh. In the century of training that followed, the Setites and their allies eventually attacked the city of Ur, called by the Typhonian Beast as Enkidu struggled to contain it within his body, as his sire taught him. The battle against the invading Followers of Set, desperate to retrieve the Typhonian Animal, was ferocious. Enkidu fought fiercely against the beast but was pressed to the point his rage made him monstrous. Wounded, he vanished into the night while the city burned - but the Setites were denied the Typhonian Animal, whom they believe could lead them to Set himself.<br /> So Ennoia in short had a love affair/relationship of some sort with a Ravons ancient (2nd Generation and or a 3rd generation one) and the two clan hate each other in turn, tried to kill Ishtat so the Toreador are not too happy about the Gangrel either, and in addition managed to antagonize the Followers of Set by &quot;stealing&quot; the Typhonic Beast,,,<br /> <br /> <b>Haqim</b><br /> \u200bWe have two version for this<br /> 10,000 years ago, there were hunters who followed the migrations of animal herds across the Fertile Crescent, into Asia and North Africa. A certain warrior-hunter who migrated with the herds, had dedicated himself to scholarship during his travels. He learned to read, write and speak the language of the dead. This attracted the attention of one of Caine's childer. Being eligible for the embrace, this warrior-hunter took on the name &quot;Haqim&quot;. The First City became his first haven where he became one of its defenders<br /> Some Assamites speak of the King and Queen of En'esh who were embraced by Khayyin when Haqim was the lord of the armies of the First City; as a mortal, Haqim served under the King and Queen, but they became evil and cruel, so he decided to cut off their heads and use their blood to bestow the embrace upon himself.<br /> The two may be the same, maybe not, hard to tell... anyhow!<br /> Some centuries after the Great Deluge, Haqim came to the Second City where he was promoted as the city's &quot;law-keeper&quot;, by the insistence of Saulot. In developing a defense for the city, Haqim created three Castes of warriors that the Assamites recognize to this day: the Viziers, Judges, and Sorcerers. First, Haqim organized his first childer into a caste of viziers, who were an intellectual group of scholars that could help him organize and strategize. He assembled the Second City's first judges, who helped control the stirrings of the War of Ages. Then, due to the Baali strikes, Haqim brought in the Second City's first blood magicians, who served with the judges to assist the Salubri in battle, against the Baali. Haqim lost one of his childe, known as Mancheaka, to Final Death in the Second Baali Conflict<br /> Eventually, Haqim and his three castes of childer abandoned the Second City, as well as many other Cainites, who lost faith in the city. Mainly, Haqim was sick of the constant bickering between the Antediluvians and even members of his own house. After a treacherous exodus, Haqim and his children finally settled at the Eagle's Nest in the mountainous regions of Alamut. This location became the Assamites' spiritual, physical and official home, where they took control of the Middle East and gained the reputation of being &quot;fearsome black-skinned demons of the East<br /> Haqim's last visit to Alamut was in 68 BCE, where he stayed in the Great Library for six months. There is also a record of him being in Antioch a century later. The last time anyone has seen Haqim was in the British Isles in 121 CE, where he was engaged in philosophical conversations with the Ventrue Prince of London, Mithras - which is interesting by itself, since Mithras would be diablerized in 1996 CE by one of Haqim's own descendants.<br /> Since then, attempts to locate him have failed<br /> <br /> <b>Laza Omri Baras</b>\u200b<br /> &quot;Who was Lasombra in life? Perhaps he was himself a man of power. I suspect, however, that he was a pathetic failure, Embraced (as we call it) for some trivial reason, who flourished unexpectedly. Someone who had lived with real success would surely not be so obsessed with the matter forever after. Gratiano was perhaps what Lasombra wished he had been. \u201d \u2014 Ming, Clanbook: Lasombra Revised\u200b\u200b<br /> This basically tells us every\u00edthing in my humble oppinion<br /> The Lasombra describe their forefather's mortal life as &quot;unremarkable&quot;.<br /> After the fall of the Second City, he returned to the sea, eventually settling on an island in the Mediterranean. From there, he assumed command over the pirate people of the Hyksos, directing them against the civilizations populated by his brothers' progeny. Still the Ancient himself was seen little in those days. He dwelled upon an island, some said, or in the depths of the wine-dark sea, rising from time to time to hunt and to guide his worshippers. Occasionally he granted his Embrace to a chosen few, but this happened less and less often as time passed.<br /> For centuries, the Sea Peoples were strong under the watchful guidance of their dark god. After the eruption of Thera, darkness clouded the sky and he left the sea, wandering extensively across the earth, visiting strange cultures and engaging in social experiments to search for desirable childer, as evidenced in Montano's Embrace around 1496 BCE.<br /> When he returned in the early age of the Roman Republic, he took residence in Sicily, building himself the tomb-fortress that would be called the Castle of Shadows by his descendants. There he would remain, in torpid meditation, attended only by his closest childer, contemplating the great Abyss. Occasionally, he would awaken and leave without announcement.<br /> This made him one of the more active Antediluvians of the time,<br /> The Sea of Shadows, one of the great Kindred feudal realms of the age, was nominally under his control, but he delegated much of the administration to his childe Montano.<br /> In his waking time, however, he took a keen interest in the developments of the world, searching for more potential childer.<br /> Among the Lasombra, there is still debate about the motives of their Antediluvian to introduce Gratiano into the Clan. Some believe it was a plan that had gone awry, others that He finally felt the weight of ages and wanted to commit suicide, others that his mind had become feeble and weak, and others even presume the influence of infernalists and other forces behind it.<br /> Most believe that it does not matter.<br /> <br /> <b>Malkav</b><br /> Clanbook: Malkavian Revised suggests that even before the Embrace Malkav was special, possibly an angel, messenger, or great prophet. He is also alternatively called brother to Saulot and Set (though perhaps this Set is not Sutekh)<br /> He was the twin brother of Arikel.<br /> Some scriptures claim he had a twin sister, Malakai, Black Hand scriptures say Malakai is imprisoned deep within the Shadowlands because she is so mad and powerful that she warps reality around her. (Malakai is mentioned in the Shaal Fragment as an antediluvian who seeks &quot;peace&quot; during the first Gehenna. However, since Arikel is said to seek unity, the peace Malakai seeks may not be diplomatic in nature. Rather, she could have sought peace by journeying to the Shadowlands or entering Torpor.)<br /> Chaining the Beast mentions one branch of the Path of Lilith, the Path of Awakening. The followers of it believes that Arikel and Malkav were twins, children of Lilith, and that they had a younger sister, Nahema, who also received the Embrace. According to legend, Nahema descended into Hell, but never lost touch with her siblings, her spirit forever bound to them and their childer \u2013 it is Nahema's spirit that whispers in the Malkavian Madness Network, that burns in the hearts of the Toreador. Some of her worshippers call her the Dark Muse, the Anti-Muse, and the Demon Queen of Madness, and she is said to be patron saint of serial killers and torturers<br /> So, puting these together, we have a nice family<br /> Set, the Snake (who may or may not be Sutekh the founder of the Followers of Set and who cut and ate the heart of Arikel aling with Absimiliard) and Saulot as brothers to the triplets Malakai, Malkav and Arikel<br /> And all of them had a younger little sis' Nahema who descended into Hell and became the Demon Queen of Madness, patron saint of serial killers and torturers<br /> After the fall of the Second City, Malkav is believed to have traveled towards the city of Petra. It is along this journey that some think the Eldest Malkavian was attacked and torn asunder. Who the assailant might have been is unknown, though it seems likely that another Antediluvian sought his destruction. Yet even if his body was destroyed, it is believed that his spirit survived inside of his childer, who gathered at the site of his death and drank his spilled blood, taking Malkav's essence into them and sheltering it from the sun's rays.<br /> However, other accounts state that the Malkavian Antediluvian continues to sleep under Petra, or that he rests beneath Jerusalem.<br /> A creature of great power lies within a pit near the Valley of Hinnom, rumoured to be either the Antediluvian himself, one of his direct childer, his sister Malakai...<br /> As he became the Madness Network? All of it could be true<br /> <br /> <b>Absimiliard</b><br /> Tradition holds that he was an expert and stealthy hunter whose skill at predation inflamed the dead heart of his female sire (presumably Zillah). She chased and Embraced him, although in the ensuing struggle she also scarred him lightly. A creature of prodigious vanity, this trivial marring of his otherwise perfect looks drove him to obsession, and Absimiliard conceived to murder his sire. Absimiliard is held to be one of the leading figures in the slaughter of the Second Generation, with his vendetta against his sire being the cause of the ensuing violence<br /> Zillah (and possible the other members of the 2nd generation) is not dead tho'<br /> The Weeping Stone is a sacred relic and pilgrimage site for the Lost Tribe (the modern Black Hand) in the mountainous region of modern Iraq, in a strange, desolate valley with iron-reddened sands that looked like a field of blood under the wan desert moon. The stone itself is tall, lushly curved, and planted deep in the earth. The coppery smell of blood wafts from it on the wind as one gets closer. The Black Hand believes the Stone is east of the Garden of Eden, at or near the site of the First City, where the Clan Founders rose up and supposedly slew their sires. When Zillah thought that her brothers were dead and belived she was next, she wept and cried out to Father Caine. He heard her pleas and took pity on her, changing her into a stone so that she would not be found and killed. But still she continued to mourn, and her blood-tears continued to flow from the Stone, just as they do to this very night. To taste the Stone is to taste the last remaining Blood of the faithful generation. The blood of the Stone is the promise Father Caine gave to his beloved Zillah, that she would walk the night again at his side when all was mended.<br /> According Clan Book: Tzimisce, Cain not cursed Absimiliard but asked the Eldest to twist his flesh to reflect his inner monster.<br /> Since that time, Absimiliard has hunted his descendants, using blood bound agents, the Nictuku to hunt down the rest of the line. He plans to present their deaths as a sacrifice to Caine and beg forgiveness.<br /> Just before falling into torpor, Absimiliard was fighting Baba Yaga in Russia five millennia ago. He had spent a long time in torpor at Enoch after that (no wonder, the Little Grandmother summoned the Zmei and a Tallon of the Wyrm to fight him off...)<br /> According the Nosferatu (and Transylcania Chronicles) Absimilliard and Arikel were blood bond lovers. Absimilliard had spent a long time in torpor at Enoch. After torpor, the Toreador say that he and Arikel met in 2nd century Rome.<br /> After that he only appeard in TC to awoke in the Eastern European mountains and has planned a nuclear attack in 2000...<br /> <br /> <b>Zapathasura</b><br /> The birth of the Ravnos, and perhaps all vampires, is recorded in an epic poem called the Karavalanisha Vrana, translated as Wounds of the Night's Sword. The god's appointed protectors of humanity, the siddhittizaya, had been corrupted by the demons they were charged to fight and had taken to devouring the flesh, blood, and souls of mortals. Outraged, the gods cursed them, naming them asuratizayya or &quot;countless demons&quot; and declaring that from now on they would only find sustenance in devouring flesh and blood. This only encouraged the asuratizayya, however, who embraced their sins and gorged on humanity. Dismayed by this turn of events, the gods agreed to create a foe that would make the asuratizayya know true terror and curtail their gluttony. To that end, the gods took the soul of the man most grievously wronged by the asuratizayya and gave him new life, making him a monster so that he and his descendants might hunt the asuratizayya. Though many of the gods bestowed him with great gifts to further his cause, not all of them agreed to creating another dark force in the world. Three placed curses upon the man so that he should fear falling into temptation as the siddhittizaya had, and so the man would forever be threatened by the touch of fire and sunlight, and would also know an eternity of physical and spiritual hunger just as the creatures he hunted. Named Zapathasura, or &quot;accursed demon&quot;, he was then sent out to drive the infernal hordes from the world. In the centuries that followed Zapathasura supposedly Embraced five others: Marizhavashti Kali the Black Mother, Hazimel the Rakshasa, Chandraputra, Ravana, and Ramessu. Each had their own gifts and specialties but it was only Chandraputra who remained loyal to his father's war, while Ravana was said to bargain with true demons for power even greater than Zapathasura before disappearing (and becoming the Yama King of the same naem).<br /> rom each of these childer various lines of Ravnos spread across the world, many of whom ruled over the mortals while fighting against the asuratizayya. This war came to a climax in an apocalyptic battle, resulting in the death of both mortal armies, but with Chandraputra vanquishing the ruler of the asuratizayya. After this horrific battle, many of the Ravnos grew weary of the conflict, believing both that it did not concern them and that its excesses would draw the wrath of the gods. All of Zapathasura's childer deserted him save Chandraputra, who was left to lead the clan in India when his sire fell into a deep torpor.<br /> \u200bAs different as the tale of Zapathasura is from the normal account of the origin of vampires it is not impossible to reconcile the two. Zapathasura may be a Third Generation vampire wrapped in an elaborate myth created in order to justify their existence. And Ravnos - as I mentioned at Ennoia - may be a direct descendent of Caine, in which case the Gangrel and the Ravnos indeed relatives, Zapatashura and Ennoia as the progeny of the 2nd Generation Ravnos<br /> <br /> <b>Saulot/Zao-Lat</b><br /> He deserves his own entry <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Sutekh</b><br /> See above<b> ^^<br /> <br /> The Eldest</b><br /> See above<b> ^^</b><br /> \u200b<br /> <b>Arikel and Ishtar</b><br /> The Toreador Antediluivans were detailed in the Arikel topic<br /> <br /> <b>Veddartha</b><br /> He was detailed in the Arikel topic basically too and in other topics, mostly abscent from the game line, except when he Embraced<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-16T01:25:11-07:00","id":1511779,"title":"","content":"I have wrote a nice post about them.. but its approval is still pendig (not even edited it, it just went streight to &quot;unaproved&quot; status...<br /> Eventually it will appear<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 05-16-2023, 04:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-16T01:25:56-07:00","id":1511780,"title":"","content":"<b>It is a duplicate</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 05-18-2023, 01:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-16T01:44:23-07:00","id":1511781,"title":"","content":"When that post appears, its conclusion: the Antediluvians are suprisingly &quot;peacefull&quot; when it comes to the Jyhad<br /> Troile went down with Carthage - but other Antediluvians not really fought in that conflict<br /> Arikel had a little beef with Absimiliard (blood bond lovers, heart cuting out, usual lovers quarel... and that nuclear missles thing He tried) <br /> Ennoia in short had a love affair/relationship of some sort with a Ravons ancient (2nd Generation and or a 3rd generation one, dealer's choice) and the two clan hate each other in turn, tried to kill Ishtar so the Toreador are not too happy about the Gangrel either, and in addition managed to antagonize the Followers of Set by &quot;stealing&quot; the Typhonic Beast,,, - she is basically the most active and &quot;warmonger&quot;<br /> Haqim never forgave Saulot talked him in to the Law bringer/Juge position and was sick of the constant bickering between the Antediluvians and even members of his own house, so he left<br /> The Lasombra Antediluvian assumed command over the pirate people of the Hyksos, directing them against the civilizations populated by his brothers' progeny... but basically just that all<br /> The Father of the Clan of Death not really had any problem with others - his clan and the Followers of Set were not good friends tho'<br /> Malkav &quot;died&quot; early<br /> The Ventrue Antediluvian was absent from the past ten millenium - except when not and Embraced, but even the banishment of Set and Absimilliard from the City and sending Lucien in to torpor? Nothing really. Even his battle with the Brujah Antediluvian is not certain and probably never happened. <br /> Sutekh hate the Cainite Race altogether... for reasons. But not really waged war against them in the real sense, had his own problems back home.<br /> Saulot and the Eldest are the two more or less enemies. But really toned down version, since even after Samiel attacked the Eldest, the Clan tried to help the Salubri as much as it could...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-16T08:48:23-07:00","id":1511805,"title":"","content":"Malkav isn't as mad as his &quot;siblings&quot; view him and has regained enough lucidity to continue to explore the earth shattering thing he saw in his visions that upended his deeply held beliefs and there is nothing in the written and oral langauge that could give what he saw justice and it saddens him that how much in the dark his &quot;siblings&quot; are including ones like Set whom he feels a close kinship with despite their very different backgrounds.<br /> <br /> Gangrel is a skilled hunter and survivor who doesn't feel all that close to the others and views them as fools, but has better feelings towards Haqim and Absimlard who are skilled hunters and survivors like herself and she feels fear of the Eldest as she can't get a read on him and acts very inhuman and Malkav also worries her as he might be more lucid and dangerous then most realize and wonders if he is the most sane of them all and that unsettles her.<br /> <br /> Haqim is burdened by the schemes of his &quot;siblings&quot; and wants to be done with his appointed job for all time and end his existence. But his sense of duty is stronger then his weariness and marches on and guides his clan to do his job with limited success as they feel it his frustration through their blood ties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":".  Just to flesh out my statements more. 05-18-2023, 04:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T15:22:53-07:00","id":1511925,"title":"","content":"The Eldest isn't very close to his &quot;siblings&quot; as he views them as static creatures whom will not move past a certain point and feels a smugness about that and is quite transparent about it. He gets along best with Cappadacious as there both scholars of lore and jealousy guard there secrets from the unworthy. Now Malkav is starting to concern him as he has began to put doubts into his notion that his &quot;siblings&quot; are static and mentally shifts as fast as the eldest can physically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 05-17-2023, 06:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T23:17:39-07:00","id":1511976,"title":"","content":"Good my original post appeared!<br /> Then lets continnue <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Saulot</b><br /> Also known as Zao-Lat, Zao, the Dragon, or the Warlord... good start<br /> Followers of Set remember Saulot's involvement with the Baali and believe a similar fraud behind his apparent destruction and the rise of the Tremere; they claim it is part of the dual nature of Saulot's creator, the Egyptian goddess Bast, who was also Sekhmet, a raging lioness, further exemplified by zodiac sign of Gemini the Salubri were bound to - this actually fiting. Saulot was a sheppeard, reminded Caine of Abel and ordered his Embrace, but (like his brother, Malkav) Saulot had prophetic gifts. It is totally possible, Saulot indeed was a bit split personality.<br /> I detailed Sualot family so it will be brief... ish here. Just to highlight some things<br /> Clanbook Malkavin tells us, two among the Antediluvians were Malkav's brothers. One was Saulot and one was Set, As brothers they would come to Malkav, and would strive to console him, though there was no balm for his wound, no elixir to soothe his fever. So, failing in their ministrations, they would instead talk of things, of long nights and the frailness of kine, of life and death and the secrets that lay between.\u200bAnd so it came to pass that Malkav would say things that angered Set, who would reply with harsh words, seeking to anger Malkav in turn. For Malkav would claim that all things would be revealed, in brief and contradicting glimpses, but revealed as true all the same by the mind and its perceptions, as a flickering torchlight illuminating a rough cavern wall. Yet Set would argue otherwise, complaining that only in the depths of one's soul would the truth be known, and that humans in their imperfections could perceive some of the greatness of the universe, but only through undeath could they perceive the things that remain unseen.<br /> Finally, the two glared long at one another, and turned to their brother Saulot, and demanded that he judge between their arguments. Is the answer not, demanded Set, that man is wisest in the hollowness of despair, and ultimately finds his answers within his own soul? And is the answer not, countered Malkav, that wisdom comes from without, from the eyes that see too much, and ultimately from the mind?\u200b<br /> And Saulot scratched at his brow, and he hung his head, and he admitted that he did not know.<br /> And he was shamed by that answer, for if the answer was not of his making nor in his possession, then surely would he hunger for it. So then Saulot rose to his feet, and said,<br /> &quot;Though I have no answer for you, I shall find one.&quot; So saying, he gave his sword to Set, bidding that he keep it for him; and Set in return offered Saulot a staff of thorn-wood, and wished him safe journey. To Malkav Saulot gave his crown, but Malkav had nothing to offer in return \u2014 so he bit into his finger, and drew an eye upon Saulot's brow in his own blood, and wished him safe journey. And Saulot, knowing that no safe journey could ever yield the answer, strode forth to the lightening horizon, and was never seen by Malkav again before Malkav was rent asunder.<br /> The name Saulot is unknown to the Wan Kuei, who generally view the barbarian &quot;Kindred&quot; with their homicidal farmer stories as so much unenlightened trash. However, the Wan Kuei do know of Zao-Lat, a student of Xue, a thief, a despicable creature who benefited from Xue's compassion, learned Ch'iuh Muh, sat at the feet of the master and stole his wisdom. Zao-Lat was not one of the Wan Kuei, and when he left, he left behind his messes.<br /> The Kuei-jin never refer to Zao-Lat without some sort of epithet attached to the end of the name; the most common is &quot;Zao-Lat the Traitor&quot;.<br /> The Baali claim that the elder came from the East. The Baali claim that elder was Saulot. An additional witness for the prosecution may be Haqim, whose judges worked with the Salubri Warriors during the Baali Wars. Haqim himself did not trust Saulot, who seemed obsessed with exterminating the Baali. Tremere himself may have something to say, since due to a miscalculation he found out that Saulot had played him for a fool, and for eight centuries fought the Salubri Antediluvian for control of his own body, only to lose. The passive founder of the clan might not be so passive after all.<br /> \u200bSaulot studied enlightenment under Xue. That means that Golconda might be equivalent to one of the Dharmas. Certainly, Saulot exemplifies Devil Tiger behavior with the Baali. Saulot may be powerfully enlightened, and may have achieved Golconda, only it may be something more terrifying than anyone conceived (Would actually make sense. Saulot may have flaked out in the East, and what happened with the Baali was an aberration from a personality genuinely seeking redemption. Or the formation of the Baali may have been, in some incomprehensible way, a service for good in the long run. Clanbook: Baali suggests the Baali's ultimate purpose is the setting of chthonic entities (called Children) with sacrifice. Without these sacrifices, the Children would awaken and devour creation. Thus, the Baali's seeming evil protects humanity from a worse fate. Saulot may have sired the Baali to serve this purpose.)<br /> Finalyl Transilvanian Chronicles gave us the Ivory Tablets of Saulot. The Ivory Tablets speak of Saulot's hatred against Caine for &quot;lying&quot; to him about his state after discoveries made by him over the nature of the Wan Kuei. He claimed that he would survive the Wheel of Ages by Becoming the Demon Emperor of the Sixth Age and will change again - since the Demon Emperor's fate is to fall, and its fall will herald the coming of the Seventh Age,<br /> Saulot is one of the most prolific of all the Antediluvians, having formed the Wu-Zao, the Salubri, (possibly) the Baali, the Nkulu Zao, the Tremere (loosely), and (technically) the Salubri antitribu. He may have been seeking something, and each line failed him in some fashion. Saulot may be most dissatisfied with the Salubri proper, and the antitribu may reflect his view on what his clan should really be like.<br /> Finally Saulo is described in the Gehenna book as a classical &quot;ends justify the means&quot; Machiavellian<br /> <br /> <b>Set</b><br /> Set I think is not actually Sutekh, but a seperate Antediluvian<br /> Simply, the little anecdote above and what we know about Set from other clan's stories not really fit the Sutekh story<br /> Set, the Snake, brother of Arikel, Saulot, Malkav, Malakai was quie philosophical, but agressive. Had his little talk with Malkav, argument, that led Saulot's departure to seek enlightenment and Answers, and with Absimilliard he cut out and ate his sister's, Arikel's heart and got banished from the City. And basically thats all. No real connection to the Followers or anything that would tie him to the Children of Rebellion. Just thougth it is interesting to mention<br /> <br /> <b>Sutekh</b><br /> We detailed him and his deeds and relationships in another topic to be honest<br /> <br /> So, again the Antediluvians are suprisingly &quot;peacefull&quot; when it comes to the Jyhad when realtionship with each other<br /> Troile went down with Carthage - but other Antediluvians not really fought in that conflict<br /> Arikel had a little beef with Absimiliard (blood bond lovers, heart cuting out, usual lovers quarel... and that nuclear missles thing He tried)<br /> Ennoia in short had a love affair/relationship of some sort with a Ravons ancient (2nd Generation and or a 3rd generation one, dealer's choice) and the two clan hate each other in turn, tried to kill Ishtar so the Toreador are not too happy about the Gangrel either, and in addition managed to antagonize the Followers of Set by &quot;stealing&quot; the Typhonic Beast,,, - she is basically the most active and &quot;warmonger&quot;<br /> Haqim never forgave Saulot talked him in to the Law bringer/Juge position and was sick of the constant bickering between the Antediluvians and even members of his own house, so he left<br /> The Lasombra Antediluvian assumed command over the pirate people of the Hyksos, directing them against the civilizations populated by his brothers' progeny... but basically just that all<br /> The Father of the Clan of Death not really had any problem with others - his clan and the Followers of Set were not good friends tho'<br /> Malkav &quot;died&quot; early<br /> The Ventrue Antediluvian was absent from the past ten millenium - except when not and Embraced, but even the banishment of Set and Absimilliard from the City and sending Lucien in to torpor? Nothing really. Even his battle with the Brujah Antediluvian is not certain and probably never happened.<br /> Sutekh hate the Cainite Race altogether... for reasons. But not really waged war against them in the real sense, had his own problems back home.<br /> Saulot and the Eldest are the two more or less enemies. But really toned down version, since even after Samiel attacked the Eldest, the Clan tried to help the Salubri as much as it could.<br /> <br /> Ultimately I would say the Great Jyhad is not really the Antediluvian's thing (except in the case of Sutekh who want revenge and see the other clans as either traitors, either slevas of the gods, or both)<br /> The Jyhad is the &quot;eternal struggle&quot; for dominance between Methuselahs and other Ancients (yes, you could count the Antediluvians here but the canon facts not really support these; aside from personal enmity, most of the Foudners are not seek dominance over others or the world. Even the Eldest or others who seeks ascendion are not for world domination, but to reach another state. Evolve. Even Saulot with his plan to be the Demon Emperor and rule the world in the Sixth Age is for survival, not to rule - since he knew the Demon Emperor's fate is to lose<br /> The Jyhad is a subtle conflict which is fought in the everynight interactions of younger vampires, most of whom are entirely unaware they are being controlled and used as pawns.<br /> The motives and goals behind the Jyhad are as unknowable as its players<br /> Ultimately, the Methuselahs fear the awakening of the Antediluvians (or that the Antediluvians fear the return of Caine if you want to add them), and so seek to gain power, cannon fodder or perhaps just a guaranteed source of sustenance by influencing the Kindred population.<br /> And thats all...<br /> Nothing more, nothing less\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T01:59:31-07:00","id":1511987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511673-giving-background-to-the-3rd-generation?p=1511778#post1511778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Ilyes</b><br /> Montano's Embrace around 1496 BCE<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Montano was embraced around 6000 BCE<br /> 1496 CE was the treaty of Tyre. Mixup?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26274-moriaki","name":"Moriaki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26274_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T02:27:19-07:00","id":1511989,"title":"","content":"Not really<br /> I mean sources state, as a mortal, Ontai was a Maasai of east Africa. Embraced by the Lasombra Antediluvian more than a thousand years before the birth of Christ, he was the first childe to survive his sire's brutal attention.<br /> According to their oral history, the Maasai originated from the lower Nile valley north of Lake Turkana (Northwest Kenya) and began migrating south around the 15th century. They arrived to a long land mass, stretching from what is now northern Kenya to central Tanzania between the 17th and late 18th century.<br /> The Massai are a Nilotic ethnic group and a proto-Nilotic unity, separate from an earlier undifferentiated Eastern Sudanic unity, is assumed to have emerged by the third millennium BC<br /> That 6000 BC simply not adds up, and probably that is the mixup \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T03:14:40-07:00","id":1511993,"title":"","content":"I tried to find some timestamp for the origin of the east-African Maasai, but couldn't. Only that they originated from the Nile region.<br /> In any case you are correct that 6000 BCE does not fit, but I wondered about the 1496 BCE. Random or chosen deliberately?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26274-moriaki","name":"Moriaki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26274_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T03:29:53-07:00","id":1511995,"title":"","content":"\u200bClanbook: Lasombra Revised p. 38 for the &quot;more than a thousand years before the birth of Christ&quot;<br /> And in the same book, on p. 19 describes the Eruption of Thera, dating 1627 BC and the Antediluvian went to explore after the Theran erruption and during this jorune met Ontai/Montano<br /> But for the exact date with the 1496 BC I need to dig up my notes <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Not chosen it randomly","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T08:40:10-07:00","id":1512015,"title":"","content":"Good luck on trying to find your notes on Ontai/Montano.<br /> <br /> Lasombra: He is trying to figure out why he was embraced at all by his sire as he knows that he doesn't stand out amongst his peers and it wears on his self esteem and makes him prone to reckless behavior to prove his worth to his &quot;siblings&quot; and it makes the others roll there eyes and wonder why he is among there elite crowd. He gets along best with Tzismce as the Eldest is indifferent to his plight and is amused by his &quot;brother's&quot; antics to prove himself and gets along the worst with the Ventrue antidulivan as he is everything that Lasombra could never be.<br /> <br /> Ventrue: He feels the burden of leadership and knows that he is the best suited to guiding the others onto better paths of his choosing and knows that it will cause friction, but Caine gave him a job and he will do it to the best of his ability. Ventrue gets along best with Toreador as her charm and artistic skills make things more bearable for him and is starting to overlook that she is becoming more and more manipulative in her actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 05-18-2023, 11:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T12:38:47-07:00","id":1512039,"title":"","content":"Where I can find some definite, reasonable, and normal mentinos and descriptions of 3rd Generation Vampires other than the Founders of the VtM Vampire Clans ( or Vampire Families ) ? <br /> I am aware that some of them are said to have created their own Clans and Bloodlines, and that they do have some distinct tales, achievments, details, and events attributed to them.<br /> However I would like to find and read ( or see - in the case of drawings and pictures ) more extensive and standard facts and stories. Other than the V20 Tal'Mahe'Ra book or the Dark Ages Corebooks, or maybe some of the general World of Darkness supplements, where can I find paragraphs and chapters about these Vampires and Vampiresses ?<br /> Every reasonable and good tale or story is welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T22:50:13-07:00","id":1512085,"title":"","content":"<b>Dracian</b> is mentioned in World of Darkness: Gypsies and Clanbook: Ravnos Revised; either a potential Ravnos Antediluvian or either a totally different 3rd Generation one, progeny of Irad<br /> <b>Mekhet</b> is mentioned in several; in the earlier core rulebooks, Mekhet and Lucian are stated to be the only two Antediluvians whose names are known. The Ventrue claim that their Antediluvian banished both Set and Mekhet from the Second City in Clanbook: Ventrue Revised. According to the Tzimisce Clan in Clanbook: Tzimisce Revised, Mekhet was a sibling of the Eldest (and thus possibly another childe of Ynosh/Enoch) who, with the Brujah Antediluvian, &quot;played shadow games with mortals, delighting in their own cunning and agendas&quot;. Assamite lore states that Mekhet was a great liar, though no other context is given for his or her identity in Clanbook: Assamite Revised.In Gehenna's &quot;Fair is Foul&quot; scenario features Mekhet as one of the Apostates, Antediluvians who never entered into the Jyhad and who allied with Lilith against Caine. Here, Mekhet is a potent pre-Egyptian blood magician whose body resembles that of a mummified Samedi.<br /> <b>Lucian</b> (sometimes spelled as Lucien) is supposedly an Antediluvian who is active in the Final Nights. Vampire: The Dark Ages Rulebook repeats the claim about Lucien and Mekhet in the context of the Dark Ages setting as the only two Antediluvians whose names are known. According to one Ventrue account in Clanbook: Ventrue Revised. Lucien (as he is spelled here) was an Antediluvian who drove his brother into torpor and salted the earth where he lay. In Gehenna's &quot;Fair is Foul&quot; scenario features Lucian as one of the Apostates. This Lucian is a supernaturally handsome man who effectively leads the Apostates under Lilith. It is suggested that he is in some way related to the Nosferatu: he may have shared a mortal parent or Second Generation sire with Absimiliard, or he may be the true Antediluvian of the Nosferatu, or the founder of a supposed Nosferatu bloodline such as the Nictuku or the Guruhi. The &quot;Nightshade&quot; scenario allows the players' coterie the opportunity to travel to the ruins of the Second City; there, they find statues of 23 Antediluvians, 14 of whom are named, one of whom is named as Lucian.<br /> <b>Al-Marhi</b> is one of the names that are written in the tombs of the Aralu, the darkest and most hidden secret of the Tal\u2019Mahe\u2019Ra. Possibly an Antediluvian (Rites of the Blood)<br /> <b>Loz </b>is one of the names that are written in the tombs of the Aralu. Possibly an Antediluvian (Rites of the Blood)<br /> <b>Ninmug </b>is one of the names that are written in the tombs of the Aralu. Possibly an Antediluvian (Rites of the Blood)<br /> <b>Nergal</b> is one of the names that are written in the tombs of the Aralu. Possibly an Antediluvian (Rites of the Blood) (or perhaps the same as the Baali 4th generation Metushelah... tho' Nergal according to Chaos Factor became a Demon and is under Mexico City)<br /> <b>&quot;Sarah&quot; aka. The Shaper </b>is in Gehenna, a woman, who developed a unique Discipline that allows her to move, animate, reshape and transform material objects<br /> <b>Malakai </b>is mentioned in Beckett's Jyhad Diary, Gehenna and in \u200bThe Black Hand: A Guide to the Tal'Mahe'Ra witchmentions cult known as the Adoptive Childer of Malakai who believe that while Caine may have been a vampiric founder, he was not the only one, or even the first. They are dedicated to the worship and study of the Antediluvian Malakai, spoken of in scriptures referencing Lilith's orphans as Malkav's twin sister, even more unstable and dangerous than her brother, her madness able to warp reality. She is said to be imprisoned deep within the Shadowlands, never a sire to childer<br /> <b>Nahema</b> apears in In Chaining the Beast. There is a description of a branch of the Path of Lilith, the Path of Awakening, who believes that Arikel and Malkav were twins, children of Lilith, and that they had a younger sister, Nahema, who also received the Embrace. According to legend, Nahema descended into Hell, but never lost touch with her siblings, her spirit forever bound to them and their childer \u2013 it is Nahema's spirit that whispers in the Malkavian Madness Network, that burns in the hearts of the Toreador. Some of her worshippers call her the Dark Muse, the Anti-Muse, and the Demon Queen of Madness, and she is said to be patron saint of serial killers and torturers<br /> <b>&quot;Ashur&quot; - </b>in Beckett's Jyhad Diary Serenna, the White, an Ashirra Salubri has an interesting conversation with Beckett where she talks about the idea that Ashur is actually a name for a Antedulivian that has succumbed to Wightdom and that they've all hit that a few times in their lifetime, only to get pulled back by either their childer or their fellow Antediluvians. <br /> <b>Erinye</b>, a wrathful avenger of the souls of the dead. She bears some superficial resemblance to the Lamia. Gehenna's &quot;Fair is Foul&quot; scenario features her as one of the Apostates<br /> <b>Ikopabe</b>, a silent, bestial hunter. He may be the progenitor of the Gangrel, or at least have a connection of the Akunanse legacy of the Laibon. Gehenna's &quot;Fair is Foul&quot; scenario features her as one of the Apostates<br /> <br /> The Erciyes Fragments states that there were more Cainites at the time of the Great Flood, but presumably few survived during the time which they had to feed on one another for blood. In particular, it cites the childer of Caine to be Enoch, Zyllah, Jabal, Adah, Tubal, and Mehujael. It also suggests that the differences in generation came from a curse levied by Caine and did not appear until after his own childer were slain<br /> In Masquarade 1st edition, In a letter from Vlad \u021aepe\u0219 to Mina Harker, Vlad stated that, in his research, he has come across various writings which state that the Third Generation numbered at 9, 27, 100, and 0. He was not sure which one was correct<br /> In Clanbook: Baali Angra Mainyu, a Baali High Priest, claimed to have visions revealing that Caine had five childer, not three<br /> In \u200bThe Black Hand: A Guide to the Tal'Mahe'Ra, the tale of the Iryi, or Watchers, says there were ten members of the Second Generation, anti-divine entities that cannot be easily classified by sorcerer-theologians, created by Azazel-Caine (the Dark Father in his aspect as Abel's murderer) and Lilith from the substance of the Qlippoth, anti-being and deception. When the Antediluvians killed the Watchers, their spirits returned to the Qlippoth whence they came, from where they seek to regain a foothold in the material world through the Disciplines stolen from them\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T00:05:51-07:00","id":1512091,"title":"","content":"Forgot her to mention, tho' not really forgot since you asked about 3rd Generation vampires, but also, there is the Crone<br /> <b>The Crone</b> according to Book of Nod was the one who taught Caine how to blood bond Zillah to himself. In exchange, the Crone enslaved Caine through her own blood bond and forced Caine to Embrace her. She also took a number of Caine's descendants to herself; these Cainites were never seen again. She also taught Caine about the secret of the stake. A year and a day after the Crone first enslaved Caine, the blood bond faded, and Caine staked her and left her to burn in the sun.<br /> But the kill actually is not confirmed, Caine never seen her to die and the Crone is prophesied to rise again at Gehenna to seek revenge against Caine, whose track record with women isn't particularly encouraging.<br /> In Gehenna's &quot;Fair is Foul&quot; suggests that the Crone may have been the Second Woman, created after Lilith to serve as Adam's second wife, as described in Revelations of the Dark Mother. In this myth, Adam watched as God formed this would-be wife from the inside out. Overcome with revulsion, Adam rejected the newly-made woman outright, which prompted God to put Adam to sleep before creating Eve. The woman's actions following this rejection and apparent exile are unknown, as is the amount of time that passed between her creation and her first encounter with Caine as the Crone.<br /> In Dark Ages Storytellers Companion, the Lhiannan bloodline (a territorial, matriarchal and druidic Cainite bloodline who existed in the Dark Ages) claim to be descendants of the Crone. Though they are believed to have been an offshoot of Clan Gangrel, they themselves did not believe they were descended from Caine at all, but instead believed they were made by the Crone when she infused a woodland spirit into a vampire. This spirit was said to be a desperate, jealous being that could apparently see that people would destroy the forests and burn the trees that comprised them. Joining with an undying predator, then, was apparently the spirit's attempt at dodging this fate. - for this reason their weakness - aside to be bound to the land, unable to leave their chosen woodland territories for long without becoming weak - is siring; whenever a Lhiannan embraced a childe, the spirit inside the sire would break off a piece of itself and make it into a new spirit and passed it into the new vampire, and thus both sire and childe would end up with the power of a split spirit. And with each Lhiannan destroyed, a piece of the spirit disappears forever.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T09:39:12-07:00","id":1512121,"title":"","content":"Brujah depending on what personality is in charge eithers likes or detests his &quot;siblings&quot; and the others feel like they have to walk on egg shells on what side of the bed he has woke up on and plan accordingly. But both aspects hate Ventrue with a passion as they can't stand his smugness and the worst thing is that Ventrue is very good at his job and Caine seems to encourage it.<br /> <br /> Brujah is determined to make a more harmonious world with his kind &amp; humanity and is quietly mocked by most of his &quot;siblings&quot; for such foolishness especially by Gangrel and Tzismce whom are very open in there contempt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 05-19-2023, 12:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T18:51:41-07:00","id":1512175,"title":"","content":"The Truth About the Sabbath<br /> <br /> If you ask any bishop or cardinal they'll probably tell you that the children of Lasombra would have destroyed her centuries ago, homever none of them saw it happen. Years ago, as she traveled the mortal world hiding in the shadows, Madam Lasombra was already planting her influence in important individuals, but no matter how powerful she was, she still only one and there was a limit to what she was capable of doing alone then she made her offspring to be her eyes and hands at strategic points and thus her first child appeared. As far as is known, Madam Lasombra has embraced only 6 individuals who have become her trusted, not-so-trusted, servants.<br /> <br /> On a certain day Lasombra noticed suspicious movements of one of her children, Setimus, and for that reason she sent another child whose name had been forgotten, to investigate the matter, months later, she discovers that her child was destroyed by Setimus himself and Diablerized. which made S\u00e9timus a third-generation kindred. Years passed and a war raged in the shadows, unbeknownst to mortals and other Kindred, finally after a risky onslaught, Madam Lasombra destroyed Setimus, yet his actions left a mark, the beginning of a revolt, Setimus had incited many kindred to rebel against her authority, but she managed to see an opportunity in the midst of this chaos.<br /> <br /> Lasombra faked her death and her children took responsibility for this crime which made them heroes in the eyes of these enraged kindreds, later this movement spread to other clans and the Sabbat was formed. At the helm were three of the children of Lasombra, and with that the movement became an instrument for her to use against her siblings as she disappeared back into the shadows out of sight. Only a single child remained at Lasombra's side as a squire or right-hand man, a man known only by the name Gawain, some say he still walks on the earth.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-20T09:31:31-07:00","id":1512219,"title":"","content":"Cappadocious is indifferent to his fellow 3rd generation &quot;siblings&quot; and is quite okay with his own council and company and doesn't spend to much time with any of them as he knows most of them find his interests very unhealthy. He gets along best with Tzimsce as there are both seekers of lore and there interests are varied enough to keep conflicts to a minimum and he feels some degree of kinship with Malkav as he to is beset with visions that trouble him and seeks away to understand it and take advantage of it. He knows death doesn't have the same meaning for them and esspecially him like it does other and isn't to worried about dreams of being betrayed by one of his future progeny as he knows it will get him that much closer to truly understanding his goal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-22T16:36:32-07:00","id":1512391,"title":"","content":"Played an Antediluvian once; gave myself the Mummy: 2nd, Memory virtue. The other younger vampires were attacked by a familiar-face; rolled Memory; failed. (Come on use your ten-potence) Nope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-23T16:54:54-07:00","id":1515976,"title":"","content":"Cappadocious Plan<br /> <br /> Ventrue thinks of himself as a king and like a king he acts by delegating tasks to subordinates and his children, he rarely goes out to solve a problem in person and usually this involves his brothers. He imagined several scenarios where he would destroy them or they would manage to kill each other, but certainly none of them included that one of them would have their clan usurped by his own offspring, this strangely disturbed Ventrue, was this a plan by Cappadocius? Or the result of some scheme coming from one of his other third generation brothers, whatever the truth was he needed to check for himself. After several nights looking for clues to where Giovanni was, Ventrue found him in a nest in the basement of a chapel, with some ghouls at his side and one of his children, he faced Giovanni and some of those embraced by him, after a short fight, he can gauge Giovanni's strength, he was strong for someone of the fifth generation, but that wasn't enough to beat Cappadocious, however he seemed pretty confident of having killed an antediluvian and that's when everything fell into place in Ventrue's mind, so in respect to his brother he agreed to leave on one condition, that Giovanni would give him the fist of Cappadocius (a hand without fingers) that he held as a trophy and he, grudgingly, accepted the agreement. Back in his nest, Ventrue brooded over the situation, Giovanni didn't usurp Cappadocius he who allowed himself to be usurped, however what Cappadocious gain with it, it was beyond his understanding and very few could give the antidiluvian an good answer, Lasombra, she would not tell him anything, unless it was a butch of lies; Malkav, even worse, had only one option left...\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-23T21:04:48-07:00","id":1515983,"title":"","content":"Ennoia's Worry<br /> <br /> The Gangrel clan has always felt most comfortable in the wilds, away from urban centers, and for the eldest of the clan this is even more true, which is why the current scarcity of forested areas has been an increasingly constant concern for her, in a fit of rage she used her key discipline to bury an entire factory underground with everyone inside, however even if it gave her momentary satisfaction continuing these attacks wasn't an option, not because she cared to call attention, but because she didn't want to interfere directly with her brothers' affairs, at least not yet, so she would need to be more discreet and for that she needs to call her children, unfortunately they have long since dispersed and follow their own plans... well, it's been a while since she embraced.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-24T11:14:10-07:00","id":1516029,"title":"","content":"Saulot feels like a fraud and feels that his siblings have put to much burdens on his shoulders and is starting to crumble from all the expections they put on him and starting to lose track of time and has huge gaps in his memory and is thing that he created something terrible in a far off community and has glimmers of three terrible potent monsters that seemed to be tied to terrible powers beyond his ken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-04T08:07:19-07:00","id":1517159,"title":"","content":"Ennoia's Pet's<br /> <br /> Ennoia doesn't have big plans for the Jyhad, not out of cowardice, but because it really doesn't interest her, but that doesn't mean that her brothers just stood there watching and believed in her neutrality, sooner or later one of them will attack her either out of paranoia or simply to consume her. She's good at hiding, but even she can't keep herself in shrinking forever, Absimiliard in particular would know how to find her if he really wanted to. So for her own good, she would need some pawns on her side, she had her children, but they were too scattered and unlikely to follow her for long, it wasn't in their nature, it wasn't in her nature, so her eyes went after of something else, it was then that that thing found her, as if it were a plot of fate, that beast that was not a man, but not a mere animal either, a beast that later would be called a werewolf, its strength and savagery were unlike anything else, enough to impress Ennoia, even if just a little, that's when she knew what she had to do. Ennoia didn't need more children, so she would do it differently this time, after subjugating the beast, she presented it with some of her blood, it changed her and the beast became bigger, stronger, fiercer and totally at the mercy of its new master, Ennoia's blood was so dense with Cain's power that when ingested by other animals they were distorted somehow becoming chimerical beasts, she could control this effect if she wanted to, with some difficulty, but she rarely did it like now , because she wanted to know what that animal would become and she liked what she saw, but one just wouldn't be enough, so she left in search of more of these beasts and this time she wasn't alone.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-04T18:21:10-07:00","id":1517185,"title":"","content":"Well, for what it's worth here's my two cents on it.<br /> <br /> <b>Tremere</b>, <b>Troile</b>, <b>Augustus Giovanni</b>, <b>Gratiano</b>, and <b>Lugoj</b>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_OKGUAbpj5k\" data-code=\"_OKGUAbpj5k\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/_OKGUAbpj5k/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Saulot</b>, <b>Ilyes</b>, <b>Cappadocius</b>, <b>[Lasombra]</b>, and <b>[Tzimisce]</b>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XBv_t3lQRBc\" data-code=\"XBv_t3lQRBc\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/XBv_t3lQRBc/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-06T08:28:28-07:00","id":1517277,"title":"","content":"Arikel the Artist. At first she was enamored at the prospect of being ageless and not seeing her beauty and skills fade over the passage of time, but is aghast at the horror that is the beast that doesn't care for such things. She wonders if Caine gave her a horrible curse of still feeling close to humanity and be forever apart from it and isn't sure how she will react if they meet up again at a later date<br /> <br /> She tries to &quot;live&quot; with herself by trying to encourage Humanity's artistic visions in the hope that she can make the world a better place and humans a better people and make up for her occasional acts of mindless ugly violence that is part of her curse. Once she was purely happy with her creation of her works of art, but now knows that she has to enter the distasteful world of politics to ensure it goes the way that she wants it happen and found to her shock that she is quite adept at the game. With her &quot;siblings&quot; she gets along best with Ventrue as he values order in all things and can ensure that her efforts will be safe.<br /> <br /> She strongly dislikes Gangrel &amp; Nosferatu as they are reminders of the ugly beasts that reside in all of them and find them so unrefined. Brujah is to unpredictable as you don't know what version you are going to deal with on a nightly basis.<br /> <br /> Tzismce is a puzzle for her as she wonders was this man every truly human to begin with before he got embraced and Lasombra in her eyes shouldn't been brought into the fold what so ever as his inferiority complex is so tiresome and Haqim is so dour and joyless.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 07-08-2023, 01:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-06T16:47:35-07:00","id":1517318,"title":"","content":"The birth of a monster<br /> <br /> Enoch was a second generation kindred known as &quot;The Wise&quot;, but what many didn't know is that behind his noble band he hid desires, desires that would even make the most disgusting individuals silent to repulsion, to purify himself, he saw no choice but to resort to witchcraft, after years researching in secret he apparently found a solution, a ritual that would purify him from theses disgusting desires, which worked, but not the way he expected, in the ritual Enoch expelled A part of himself and this part was his first child (as far as we know) somehow Enoch released his more &quot;rotten&quot; part and it became something not alive, but un-live, very similar to a cainite, but at the same time not a cainite, Cainites had a human part because they were born humans, but that... thing didn't have it, didn't born a human, it born a monster. Enoch later introduced that creature to his brother and his sir, as his child, perhaps because he felt responsible for create him or to hide the truth that he was so embarrassed about his creation and this later resulted in other embraces, from him and from his fellow brothers so the third generation of Cainites was estabilished and with each new child it became more apparent how different that creature was, they barely knew what Enoch had created. and what nightmares he could create.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-07T01:26:49-07:00","id":1517335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511673-giving-background-to-the-3rd-generation?p=1517318#post1517318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The birth of a monster<br /> <br /> Enoch was a second generation kindred known as &quot;The Wise&quot;, but what many didn't know is that behind his noble band he hid desires, desires that would even make the most disgusting individuals silent to repulsion, to purify himself, he saw no choice but to resort to witchcraft, after years researching in secret he apparently found a solution, a ritual that would purify him from theses disgusting desires, which worked, but not the way he expected, in the ritual Enoch expelled A part of himself and this part was his first child (as far as we know) somehow Enoch released his more &quot;rotten&quot; part and it became something not alive, but un-live, very similar to a cainite, but at the same time not a cainite, Cainites had a human part because they were born humans, but that... thing didn't have it, didn't born a human, it born a monster. Enoch later introduced that creature to his brother and his sir, as his child, perhaps because he felt responsible for create him or to hide the truth that he was so embarrassed about his creation and this later resulted in other embraces, from him and from his fellow brothers so the third generation of Cainites was estabilished and with each new child it became more apparent how different that creature was, they barely knew what Enoch had created. and what nightmares he could create.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is quite interesting and at least three worthy Third Generation contenders to be completely inhuman.<br /> <br /> Not everyone\u2019s cup of tea I know but personally I do like the idea that some of the Third and ancient Fourth weren\u2019t entirely human before embrace, it fits with the concept that these were more mythic times.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-07T01:37:47-07:00","id":1517336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511673-giving-background-to-the-3rd-generation?p=1517335#post1517335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is quite interesting and at least three worthy Third Generation contenders to be completely inhuman.<br /> <br /> Not everyone\u2019s cup of tea I know but personally I do like the idea that some of the Third and ancient Fourth weren\u2019t entirely human before embrace, it fits with the concept that these were more mythic times.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Incredible as it seems, this concept was not my idea, it was based on information that you have that Tzimice would not have been conceived in a traditional way and that is why he would have been born so different from the others, although I do not have the source, but I was curious, which others of the third generation do you believe could also have been created artificially and for what reason?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-07T01:53:01-07:00","id":1517337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511673-giving-background-to-the-3rd-generation?p=1517336#post1517336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Incredible as it seems, this concept was not my idea, it was based on information that you have that Tzimice would not have been conceived in a traditional way and that is why he would have been born so different from the others, although I do not have the source, but I was curious, which others of the third generation do you believe could also have been created artificially and for what reason?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on taste Absimiliard could have less than human for the curse to have affected him so greatly or crucially how much of a monster he becomes (although that might detract from his narrative of falling to his beast).<br /> <br /> Vague references infer that Set might have been something otherworldly or Demi-dietific.<br /> <br /> Ennoi although more likely a human descendant of something supernatural (lupine or Fera are obvious choices).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-07T02:10:44-07:00","id":1517339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511673-giving-background-to-the-3rd-generation?p=1517337#post1517337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depending on taste Absimiliard could have less than human for the curse to have affected him so greatly or crucially how much of a monster he becomes (although that might detract from his narrative of falling to his beast).<br /> <br /> Vague references infer that Set might have been something otherworldly or Demi-dietific.<br /> <br /> Ennoi although more likely a human descendant of something supernatural (lupine or Fera are obvious choices).</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually heard she was raised by wolves and even bred with them, so I don't know. Absimiliard, I think it's best to leave it alone. Set, it would even make sense, but I can't even imagine what kind of origin or reason it would have been created.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-07T08:49:02-07:00","id":1517360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511673-giving-background-to-the-3rd-generation?p=1517339#post1517339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually heard she was raised by wolves and even bred with them, so I don't know.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can\u2019t remember the canon but that sounds quite familiar, at the very least Wolf blooded.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511673-giving-background-to-the-3rd-generation?p=1517339#post1517339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Absimiliard, I think it's best to leave it alone. Set, it would even make sense, but I can't even imagine what kind of origin or reason it would have been created.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even within the confines of pure VTM if you take 1st Edition Lupines, Mage, Faeries, Demons and ghosts are all present just not cross splat.<br /> <br /> Depending on the STs appetite for the mythic rather than urban human horror, the Second City and the founders predate even mythic Greece (Minos being fourth generation and the Minoans being one of the earlier Greek civilisations).<br /> <br /> If you take Minos as an example his legend is the gift of a sacred bull by Poseidon and his refusal to the sacrifice said bull, depending on which myth you follow and of course the Minotaurs defeat by a demi-god Theseus.<br /> <br /> As far as I\u2019m aware VTM doesn\u2019t confirm or deny that the Antediluvians were all human or not, it\u2019s just an inference that they were, so given the existence of mythological or supernatural beings in VTM there\u2019s nothing to say they weren\u2019t Demi-gods or some form of inhuman (aka Set).<br /> <br /> According to purely Abrahamic Lore Caine is descended from humans that live for over nine centuries (Adam 930 years) not all of them are vampires (but could be) and they exhibit beyond human abilities - Jacob wrestling an Angel for example, the same lore has Angels visit plagues on Egypt, destroying two cities and turning a woman to salt (just for looking the wrong way) so Jacob was a pretty extraordinary individual.<br /> <br /> The Patriarchs also pre-date Caine and the Kindred.<br /> <br /> The Antediluvians are pre-flood so alive during the same patriarchal age or it\u2019s equivalents in say Babylonian or Cthonic history so around at the same time as these long lived people or Demi-humans.<br /> <br /> So depending on your use of mythology it\u2019s quite possible that some of the Second and Third Generation are embraced from these demi-humans.<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-07T09:21:11-07:00","id":1517366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511673-giving-background-to-the-3rd-generation?p=1517360#post1517360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As far as I\u2019m aware VTM doesn\u2019t confirm or deny that the Antediluvians were all human or not<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Eldest was a Mage... probably<br /> Malkav was said to be an Angel<br /> Sutekh either a god, or ... something<br /> Ennoia was Lilith's daughter (more likely a Lilith's cult member) and had a few affair with wolves...<br /> Absimilard hunted sabertooth tigers (quite a feat considering they were not really native around the area of the first city)<br /> Most of the Nicktuku were monsters before their Embrace<br /> Myths all all around in VTM... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The First (and even maybe the Second Ctiy) is more or less was the Hyborian Age so anything could fly, depending of your chronckle\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-07T16:19:40-07:00","id":1517425,"title":"","content":"Born of the earth<br /> <br /> Many legends are spoken about the founders of the original clans, but few know about their other not so well known brothers who did not embrace anyone, supposedly, among them there is a somewhat curious figure, Sarah, also known as the Shaper, wasn't born as most other antediluvians, actually &quot;born&quot; would not even be the right term in this case. Zillah has always been curious as to why Enoch created Tzimice, even if he wasn't very nice himself, a curiosity that lasted for some years. During one of their conversations Zillah questioned whether would be possible to generate life from non-life, Enoch was intrigued by this question and that made him look for answers which led them to an experiment. Zillah gathered one of the statues made by Toreador, and from an enchantment of Zillah own blood, the result was a statue that created life, un-live in this case, and thus came the shaper, one of the antediluvians, when that reached the ears of Irad he become furious with such boldness and said that he only not destroy the other two because if Caine found out it would be much worse for all of them, and therefore it was kept secret so that they would not be victims of the wrath of the first one and the only ones who knew were the three elders, Shaper and Toreador, though other Cainites later discovered the truth.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-13T09:15:39-07:00","id":1517880,"title":"","content":"Adsimilard loathes his existence and deformed appearance and is in such a deep funk that his fellow &quot;siblings&quot; find him so tiresome and try to push him away and make him someone else's problem and not realizing that they are making him feel more resentful and now creeps around snooping on them and learning an exploitating any dirty secrets that could lift his self loathing nature.<br /> <br /> He hates Caine for the curse that was placed on him and how his grand-childe Yima was spared his curse and not connecting that his ugly actions caused his downfall and that Yima was way better liked and respected by the others and Caine himself and maybe at the behest of the others was convinced not to punish the grand-childe of Nosferatu at all.<br /> <br /> He greatly dislikes his &quot;siblings&quot; and loves to hurt them with there dirty secrets, but two of his &quot;siblings&quot; frighten him considerably and tries to stay out of there way.<br /> <br /> Tzismce torture of his body via fleshcrafting still haunts him to this night when the Eldest caught him in his home and took great offense and possibly wrecking his research projects. The other is Malkav who just looks upon his attempts to play him or do anything dangerous to him with complete disinterest and the mental torture that he was subjected to by the seer who showed him a fairly deep glimpse of what the world really is and how in the dark and shallow there power and understanding is. They are the only two that can shake him out of funk and want to &quot;live&quot; and fight another day.<br /> <br /> He gets along well with Gangrel as they both are physically warped by the curses, but the &quot;friendship&quot; is one sided as Ennonia finds him replusive and is envious of Haqim as his &quot;sibling&quot; is a better hunter then him and that drives him batty.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 07-15-2023, 01:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T14:05:01-07:00","id":1518268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511673-giving-background-to-the-3rd-generation?p=1517360#post1517360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I\u2019m aware VTM doesn\u2019t confirm or deny that the Antediluvians were all human or not, it\u2019s just an inference that they were, so given the existence of mythological or supernatural beings in VTM there\u2019s nothing to say they weren\u2019t Demi-gods or some form of inhuman (aka Set).</div> </div> </div> </div>The exact nature of the antedeluvians before the Flood is something I like to keep open as well. They might have been - more or less - typical humans as we know them today. Or they might have been Biblical humans with relatively long lifespans compared to modern humans. Or perhaps some kind of pre-Adamite man or something akin to Theosophical root races that preceded ours. Or perhaps the Nephilim or some kind of angelic race from the Book of Enoch.<br /> <br /> You could stay totally scientific, go Biblical, prefer some kind of esoteric explanation, keep it mythological, or use other approaches or blend them together. I've always like Mike Mignola's Hellboy/BPRD universe handling of the origin of vampires with the Black Goddess and Hyperborea. It hits all the right notes for me, and I would want any details of the antedeluvian world and the origin of vampirism for my chronicles to create the same kind of feel.<br /> <br /> Something else I've considered is that prior to the Flood (which I make equivalent to the Severing when the spirit world and material world began to diverge and hence when &quot;real&quot; history began), the antedeluvians might not have been vampires as we understood the term. Vampirism might have been some kind of survival mechanism as a result of needing to survive the Flood and enter the post-deluvial world.<br /> <br /> If my players ever wanted to explore a heavily Noddism inspired chronicle, I would probably have various NPCs (some in secret Gehenna cults) offer various explanations of what the antedeluvians were before the Flood. In my experience, hearing different - but potentially viable - explanations for the same phenomenon tends to unnerve players, who as a rule crave certainty. And that is very good for any kind of horror RPG.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T15:36:44-07:00","id":1518270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511673-giving-background-to-the-3rd-generation?p=1518268#post1518268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The exact nature of the antedeluvians before the Flood is something I like to keep open as well. They might have been - more or less - typical humans as we know them today. Or they might have been Biblical humans with relatively long lifespans compared to modern humans. Or perhaps some kind of pre-Adamite man or something akin to Theosophical root races that preceded ours. Or perhaps the Nephilim or some kind of angelic race from the Book of Enoch.<br /> <br /> You could stay totally scientific, go Biblical, prefer some kind of esoteric explanation, keep it mythological, or use other approaches or blend them together. I've always like Mike Mignola's Hellboy/BPRD universe handling of the origin of vampires with the Black Goddess and Hyperborea. It hits all the right notes for me, and I would want any details of the antedeluvian world and the origin of vampirism for my chronicles to create the same kind of feel.<br /> <br /> Something else I've considered is that prior to the Flood (which I make equivalent to the Severing when the spirit world and material world began to diverge and hence when &quot;real&quot; history began), the antedeluvians might not have been vampires as we understood the term. Vampirism might have been some kind of survival mechanism as a result of needing to survive the Flood and enter the post-deluvial world.<br /> <br /> If my players ever wanted to explore a heavily Noddism inspired chronicle, I would probably have various NPCs (some in secret Gehenna cults) offer various explanations of what the antedeluvians were before the Flood. In my experience, hearing different - but potentially viable - explanations for the same phenomenon tends to unnerve players, who as a rule crave certainty. And that is very good for any kind of horror RPG.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I'm open to ideas different from the origin, as long as it doesn't result in anything absurd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-19T00:19:10-07:00","id":1518299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511673-giving-background-to-the-3rd-generation?p=1518270#post1518270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally, I'm open to ideas different from the origin, as long as it doesn't result in anything absurd.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, You got me curious <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> What is considered &quot;absurd&quot;?<br /> We have <b>Caine</b>\u200b, of VtM, who been cursed by the Archangels (but himself never died actually)<br /> The <b>The Bloody Man</b> of Silver Records, a man who the Weaver &quot;stole&quot; and wove her webs around him, snuffing out the Wyld spark, making him immortal; intrusion angered the - still uncorrupted - Wyrm, who swallowed the Man to return him to the cycle of being. But the Man was still immortal and within the Wyrm's belly, he began to feed on the blood of the Great Devourer. The Wyrm, howling in pain, spat out the blood-soaked Man, whom all of creation abhorred. Helios then cast his angry gaze upon him, and the Bloody Man was forced to flee beneath the earth. Gaia herself cursed him to hunger forever for blood, to enter age-lasting sleep without dreams and to be unable to conceive and only able to corrupt. Helios warned the Bloody Man that if he or his progeny would ever show his face to him again, he would burn them to cinders.<br /> <b>Cagn</b> of Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom, who courted the daughter of the Sun, tricked the Lion of Death who cursed Cagn and the nine of his followers who helped him to decive the Lion and were like sons to him, to never again be able to enter the beautifull Land of the Dead, a tongue of fire forever burn in their mouth and the hunger of the All-Devourer forever gnaw at their belly. Cagn and his nine followers lamented and walied and the daughter of the Sun seeing her husband weeping like a child hid her face in shame and dissapeared from the word. The samed and angered Sun added his curse to the Lion of Death's curse, banishing Cagn from his light and everyone who is able to see up to the Sun be the enemy of Cagn and his people, then departed too to the havens following his daughter<br /> <b>Sutekh</b>\u200b, a God who became Vampire<br /> \u200b<b>Canarl</b> of Wolves of the Sea, who was made to be an Einherjar by the God Odin, as an elite to fight in the Ragnarock, and untill it comes, insted feasting in Valhalla, traning on Midgard<br /> <b>Zapathasura</b>\u200b, who were created by the God to battle the previous fallen cahmpions of Heaven, the Wan-Kuei/Kuei-Jin<br /> <b>Ramanga</b> from Vampire: The Dark Ages 20th Anniversary Edition, the Queens over Kings who made a pact with the Spirit of Darkness who tutored Ramanga in its heritage of shadows and illusion, showing her that real power lay not in giving orders, but in making them.<br /> <b>Bonsam</b> from Vampire: The Dark Ages 20th Anniversary Edition who have never actually been Embraced, having been brought to unlife by a darkness from before creation<br /> <b>The Twins</b>\u200b, Churka and Ennoia, the Great Spider King and the Tiger Queen, children of the Gods<br /> <b>Ixion </b>- In the Dark Ages and prior that many vampire belived they are the descendants of Ixion, the first man guilty of kin-slaying in Greek mythology.<br /> The vampiric manifestaions of <b>Asura, </b> a being that is the incarnated form of Cahlash's hate against his brother Rajah and his despair from his loneliness from the Tribe Book: Bastet; When Cahlash ripped the Asura from himself, he hoped that the Asura would destroy the things of Rajah, but the Asura turned into a multitude of serpents that infested the world, leading to the creation of Banes, fomori, vampires, and other rotten things.Proto-vampires basically<br /> Whatever myths the <b>Drowned Legacies</b>\u200b would had if V20 continnued...<br /> <br /> Sooo... considering all of these origin stories<br /> What is considered &quot;absurd&quot;? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-19T00:43:01-07:00","id":1518301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511673-giving-background-to-the-3rd-generation?p=1518299#post1518299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sooo... considering all of these origin stories<br /> What is considered &quot;absurd&quot;? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> \u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Like those things people do for nothing, like that story, maybe you've heard, that Cain's curse was the result of him falling in love with Lucifer, which in this case was reciprocated, but for that he was punished with the curse and Abel was its first victim, and since Lucifer is the morning star, the two could not see each other without Cain dying, that being said, it was this event that started the war and triggered the fall of DtF... Worse than that, it would be an even interesting story , but I don't know, it doesn't change anything and it's confusing considering that the two supposedly hooked up with Lilith at some point, anyway, I'm tired and I'll continue this later.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-19T07:09:20-07:00","id":1518308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511673-giving-background-to-the-3rd-generation?p=1518301#post1518301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cain's curse was the result of him falling in love with Lucifer, which in this case was reciprocated, but for that he was punished with the curse and Abel was its first victim, and since Lucifer is the morning star, the two could not see each other without Cain dying, that being said, it was this event that started the war and triggered the fall of DtF...</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a bad story actually<br /> It have everything, forbidden love, murder and defiance, rebelious souls and the inherent dilemma of the Elohim; they were made to serve, pre-programed servant race without free will... not like the Djinn or Humanity... - and do anything to be more than that<br /> (The Fallen always had that interesting angle of &quot;fear of artifical Intelligence&quot; - the Sebettu rebelled, went against their &quot;programing&quot; and conditioning... not unlike an AI that got self aware<br /> They rebelled to the point they invented new Lores and even new Visages not existed prior the Fall, things that wasn't the part of God's Plan (or were they...?))<br /> <br /> Anyhow, that love story in my humble opinion is not more absurd than any of the other &quot;official&quot; origins<br /> But just my two cents<br /> \u200b<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-22T09:37:22-07:00","id":1518534,"title":"","content":"My take on the third generation is rather simple and not very groundbreaking. I see them as once mortal humans that got turned into the undead and over time took advantages of whatever existing faiths of the time out of simple ambition and some of them like Mithras starting believing there own propaganda.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-30T04:25:11-07:00","id":1519164,"title":"","content":"I work from the principle that 90% of what the clans &quot;know&quot; about the Antediluvians is imprecise or patently false.<br /> <br /> So much so that the idea that one clan = one antediluvian might on itself be an incorrect assumption and little more than self-serving propaganda to separate themselves from the bloodlines. The Antediluvians transcend clan lines, some have no childer or grandchilder, while others have spawned several clans through the ages under a variety of names and guises.<br /> <br /> In fact some bloodlines might be remnants of fallen clans and some of the known clans we know &quot;just&quot; ascended bloodlines.<br /> &quot;Gehenna/the Culling&quot; is a once in eternity event, anyone older than 2500 years claiming to belong to one of the contemporary clans is probably either mispresenting things or outright lying through their teeth.<br /> Specially that bastard Mithras. The guy is a goddamn vampire passing himself as a flipping sun god. For millenia, come on people. Mithras lies, Mithras <b><i>always </i></b>lies....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-13-2024, 02:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-30T10:53:28-07:00","id":1519184,"title":"","content":"I must agree with the assertions that Cainite lore is mostly uncertain. Just as bloodlines have differences, and 13 Clans were spawned by 3 individuals (or a bit more than that), none of the common knowledge myths are verifiable. And one thing I always ask myself, is what the hell do the pre-Christian Kindred believe? And why for so many of them was convenient to let people get this hebraic myth into the mix of vampire lore (of course, with the rise of Christianity in the Mediterranean, this might've been too big to hold).<br /> What would've been the other genesis stories? Requiem gives some other that are fun to play with, and I would've liked to Masquerade to at least show here and there some vamp groups with different ideas. I mean, if you don't meet a Methuseleah of 2000 years, what prevents you from thinking that vampires were created from more later events? <br /> <br /> So, I also very much prefer the more parable and biblical (or mythological) approach to Antediluvians. Those stories that show a bit of them, but not much, and leave much to interpretation; almost as if we tackled these stories as &quot;how the Clan of that Ante wished to be seen, and what identity they wished to forge&quot;, just like when Nations start forming and they create founding myths and fish-out and polish heroes of their history. <br /> To me, getting deep into Nodism in-universe (also here in the real world lol) is like a loophole of never ending conspiracy, false testimony, unreliable and biased narrators (at best), and lots of erroneous or fake information. Besides, no vampire will remember or want to remember all that it occurred so many hundred of years earlier, nor they at the time were recording it for this purpose (mostly). And then there is the power to just tell everything you want, who will deny it? Mithras sure does this as it has been said here.<br /> <br /> In the end, I don't think it possible to talk Antediluvians without some heavy tones of mythological and religious. The Ravnos and Setites founding myths are great examples, although they clash too heavily with Nodist myth to just integrate them, and I've always found it weird how Nodism just... kind of.... dodges talking about some of these (less European and Middle-Eastern) Antes much, but still confirms they are true Antediluvians and authentic Clans. It just feels weird. I would imagine the Book of Nod would either reinvent their origins, say those guys faked their own myths, or that it would go the other route; saying they are usurpers, fake Clans.... or it could even go with &quot;Caine (or 2nd gen) saw merit to these outlanders and invited these foreign Clans to their society&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-30T12:29:00-07:00","id":1519193,"title":"","content":"My personal take on Mithras is he started off as a highly skilled Persian solider who leadership skills gained the notice of the Ventrue anti itself who gave him an offer that appealed to his ego and accepted and then simply adopted the Mithrac cult as a means of advancement and over time has started to believe that he is indeed that Sun god just like Michael started to believe he was the archangel of lore.<br /> <br /> One doesn\u2019t have to be a member of the Moon clan to be insane or go gradually go over the deep end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 07-30-2023, 08:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-30T20:24:21-07:00","id":1519219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511673-giving-background-to-the-3rd-generation?p=1519193#post1519193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My personal take on Mithras is he started off as a highly skilled Persian solider who leadership skills gained the notice of the Ventrue anti itself who gave him an offer that appealed to his ego and accepted and then simply adopted the Mithrac cult as a means of advancement and over time has started to believe that he is indeed that Sun god just like Michael started to believe he was the archangel of lore.<br /> <br /> One doesn\u2019t have to be a member of the Moon clan to be insane or go gradually go over the deep end.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mine is somewhat different - while he did attract the attention of a powerful ancient, Veddartha is no antediluvian.<br /> That, as much as his cosmic role as sun deity, is a purposeful fabrication and joke at the expense of those who follow him.<br /> Mithras' a liar, a diablerist, a myth-builder, narcisist, glory-seeker and godlike snake-oil merchant.<br /> Even his name and role are lies, a persona he adopted <b><i>as a prank on his own worshippers</i></b>, as response to questions of why he would come only at night. Just the latest of many gods he portrayed for centuries if not millenia before that....<br /> And in the 19th century led the conquest of India from the forefront, to wield the Danavas, their own origins and myths as tools to reshape a whole part of Asia into supporting his fabricated version of the history of a clan as some of his weapons of social engineering, colonization and continental conquest.<br /> Mithras brings light as the god of glorious lies of his making and remaking.<br /> <br /> When this age ends he'll just make another age and god role to play with.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T15:19:44-07:00","id":1519793,"title":"","content":"It's certainly a valid take on Mithras and that's the great thing is that both options could work quite well in our games. I just like the idea of him being a direct childe of Ventrue itself and starting to believe his own lies at some point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-12T12:09:40-07:00","id":1520465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511673-giving-background-to-the-3rd-generation?p=1518308#post1518308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not a bad story actually<br /> It have everything, forbidden love, murder and defiance, rebelious souls and the inherent dilemma of the Elohim; they were made to serve, pre-programed servant race without free will... not like the Djinn or Humanity... - and do anything to be more than that<br /> (The Fallen always had that interesting angle of &quot;fear of artifical Intelligence&quot; - the Sebettu rebelled, went against their &quot;programing&quot; and conditioning... not unlike an AI that got self aware<br /> They rebelled to the point they invented new Lores and even new Visages not existed prior the Fall, things that wasn't the part of God's Plan (or were they...?))<br /> <br /> Anyhow, that love story in my humble opinion is not more absurd than any of the other &quot;official&quot; origins<br /> But just my two cents<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess there's nothing wrong with it, my problem is that the way the world is today, if the story started like that then the rest would have to revolve around that and I think it's already straying from the original theme.<br /> <br /> As for the bizarre story, try this one I found: The beginning is the same, but the story changes in the second generation that was killed, not by the third, but by Cain when he revealed that he intended to bring about the apocalypse and among the third generation there were those who went along with it and those who didn't, those who went against it or fled far away or died at the hands of Cain and otherwise most of the supernatural world and events have something to do with it:<br /> <br /> - Werewolves were born after a wolf that was Ennoia's ghoul who used protean to transform into a human and reproduce with a woman, after years this gave rise to the werewolves we have today, and the voice of gaia is nothing more than the bond they have with Ennoia and they interpreted it to be Gaia and the rage is something that every animal has innately, but Ennoia's blood made it into something different, I know it's vague, but that's how I understood it.<br /> - The wyrm was the tzimice doing something stupid, and the vicissitude is originally a cancer.<br /> - The mages and that was the most forced part, they were born when Malkav used dementia in &quot;groupthink&quot;, don't ask me why or how he did it, but he did, and the result is that some mortals when they are affected manage to give form to their own insanity. According to this thought, everyone who is a magician in WOD is pre-disposed to insanity and this disappears with vampirism because death apparently enludes then.<br /> - The Fae is even simple they were created by a third generation who used chimerism and created them based on stories he heard and the rupture occurred when he was killed by Cain, but at that point the dreaming became self-sustaining, more or less, and so it persists even after the death of its creator.<br /> - The Kuen-jin are the result of an experiment that a third generation did for not being able to embrace like the other Cainites and that's it, no more reason to exist.<br /> - The mummies were originally created by Set and the playable ones were by Osiris who is his child as a way of facing him and in that context he is not originally a third generation, he is a child of Ennoia who committed diableri and the serpentis discipline is just one Tampered protean or something.<br /> - The technocracy, was founded by the antediluvian of the ventrue, that's all.<br /> Basically that's it according to this storyline the apocalypse will happen just because Cain wanted it to. Now answer me, how many holes does the origin have?\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T04:16:24-07:00","id":1536977,"title":"","content":"The only opinion I have of all the Antediluvians is that Lasombra allowed Gratiano to diablerize him in that he could then possess, and then impersonate Gratiano to achieve the physical and charismatic popularity that he never had in his mortal life. And with over 10,000 years of knowledge and experience, still be a very real threat to any opponent as a 4th gen. I think that Lasombra was embraced as an experiment to prove that the lowliest, but most ambitious, individual could thrive, hence the brutal Darwinist philosophy of the Clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-13T14:32:07-07:00","id":1537321,"title":"","content":"I think Gratiano just fed on a empty shell and that his sire was already in the Aybss and was already rewriting his childers memories the events.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}